00:10:34.703 --> 00:10:37.634
tryin' to actually do that
idea, before Media Temple.

00:10:37.634 --> 00:10:39.344
The funny thing, is that
I have a million bucks,

00:10:39.344 --> 00:10:41.724
so I had to actually
borrow a million bucks,

00:10:41.724 --> 00:10:45.715
and I spent it on business
partners, who moved really slow,

00:10:45.715 --> 00:10:48.054
and really wanted the best that they did.

00:10:48.054 --> 00:10:50.893
Within 12 months, we launched nothing.

00:10:50.893 --> 00:10:53.613
They also had some of the
problems, in my previous slide,

00:10:53.613 --> 00:10:56.338
right, like financial instability,

00:10:56.338 --> 00:10:59.083
and they had a family, and
kids, of I think like, six?

00:10:59.083 --> 00:11:00.862
So, I even bought 'em a
home in Rockwell, Texas,

00:11:00.862 --> 00:11:03.526
that cost 200 and something thousand.

00:11:03.526 --> 00:11:05.155
Why did I buy it, instead of renting it?

00:11:05.155 --> 00:11:08.615
I have no clue, I was stupid and young.

00:11:08.615 --> 00:11:12.480
But nonetheless, I lost
over a million bucks,

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.580
on that, of borrowed money.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:15.551
Not investor money, but borrowed money,

00:11:15.551 --> 00:11:18.140
that I had to pay back.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:19.771
And it failed miserably,

00:11:19.771 --> 00:11:21.670
because we never launched anything.

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:23.011
If you can't launch something,

00:11:23.011 --> 00:11:25.121
someone like me, the tumble's
going to beat you to the punch,

00:11:25.121 --> 00:11:27.701
get a ton of customers,
and make a lot of money.

00:11:27.701 --> 00:11:29.631
So, lessons I learned from that,

00:11:29.631 --> 00:11:32.432
set deadlines, no matter what.

00:11:32.432 --> 00:11:33.697
You have to set deadlines.

00:11:33.697 --> 00:11:36.545
People have to be held
accountable to 'em as well, right?

00:11:36.545 --> 00:11:39.978
Can't just set a deadline,
it passes, nothing happens,

00:11:39.978 --> 00:11:41.449
someone better be meeting 'em.

00:11:41.449 --> 00:11:44.038
If not, you know, something has to change.

00:11:44.038 --> 00:11:46.149
You also need to make sure they're small.

00:11:46.149 --> 00:11:48.978
At the deadline, if the milestones, goals,

00:11:48.978 --> 00:11:51.269
are too big for those deadlines,

00:11:51.269 --> 00:11:52.549
they're not going to get met.

00:11:52.549 --> 00:11:55.288
So, make 'em really small, and tangible.

00:11:55.288 --> 00:11:58.589
That way, you can see it,
really well in advance,

00:11:58.589 --> 00:12:01.140
if they're actually
going to be met, or not.

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:04.060
And last, but not least,
don't worry about perfection.

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:05.647
A lot of people, like dude,

00:12:05.647 --> 00:12:08.689
I'm going to create the
most perfect version of,

00:12:08.689 --> 00:12:10.228
you know, whatever it may be.

00:12:10.228 --> 00:12:11.508
That software has a lot of buzz.

00:12:11.508 --> 00:12:12.849
Mine's going to be perfect.

00:12:12.849 --> 00:12:13.960
Perfection is overrated.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:14.979
Nothing is ever perfect.

00:12:14.979 --> 00:12:16.369
You're going to continue
to have to iterate

00:12:16.369 --> 00:12:17.379
so forth, and so on.

00:12:17.379 --> 00:12:18.729
It's never going to be perfect.

00:12:18.729 --> 00:12:19.968
There's always going to be issues.

00:12:19.968 --> 00:12:21.019
Just get it out there,

00:12:21.019 --> 00:12:22.598
and start tryin' to make money.

00:12:22.598 --> 00:12:23.518
- I think, you famously said,

00:12:23.518 --> 00:12:25.300
strategy is five percent of the answer,

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.489
and execution is 95 percent?

00:12:27.489 --> 00:12:29.239
So, what does that mean,

00:12:29.239 --> 00:12:31.766
and how did you actually,
what did you do differently?

00:12:31.766 --> 00:12:33.011
- [Carlos] You know, the five percent,

00:12:33.011 --> 00:12:34.779
yeah, I said...

00:12:34.779 --> 00:12:36.758
Five percent of a challenge, is strategy,

00:12:36.758 --> 00:12:38.517
and 95 percent of the execution.

00:12:38.517 --> 00:12:41.998
This, I said it, as a CEO of Nissan.

00:12:41.998 --> 00:12:43.617
I said it, also, as CEO of Renault,

00:12:43.617 --> 00:12:46.636
and I said it, as deputy CEO of Renault.

00:12:46.636 --> 00:12:49.347
When I said it the first
time, it was mainly in France.

00:12:49.347 --> 00:12:53.514
And I was, to the top management
of Renault, in France,

00:12:54.385 --> 00:12:56.916
because there was a
tendency, in the company,

00:12:56.916 --> 00:12:58.626
to spend too much time on strategy,

00:12:58.626 --> 00:13:02.038
and leave the execution for other people.

00:13:02.038 --> 00:13:04.404
And this is where I said,
yeah, strategy is fine,

00:13:04.404 --> 00:13:05.710
it's very important.

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.411
But, it's only five percent.

00:13:07.411 --> 00:13:10.180
If you don't go to execution after this,

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.119
the delivery, and the
performance of the company

00:13:12.119 --> 00:13:13.329
is going to be very weak.

00:13:13.329 --> 00:13:15.010
I really, I really believe it.

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:17.021
Now, it doesn't mean that
strategy's not important,

00:13:17.021 --> 00:13:18.929
but when you establish north,

00:13:18.929 --> 00:13:23.278
and you know exactly where
north is, for the company,

00:13:23.278 --> 00:13:24.623
you've done something very important,

00:13:24.623 --> 00:13:26.155
because you're giving the direction.

00:13:26.155 --> 00:13:28.074
But, if you don't stop moving north,

00:13:28.074 --> 00:13:32.250
if you don't stop mapping,
and establishing milestone,

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.021
you're never going to be getting there.

00:13:34.021 --> 00:13:35.432
You're never going to be getting there.

00:13:35.432 --> 00:13:38.041
- People start what if-ing
themselves, alright?

00:13:38.041 --> 00:13:39.872
They say, aw I got this great idea,

00:13:39.872 --> 00:13:43.022
but what if I do all this
work, and it doesn't work?

00:13:43.022 --> 00:13:44.482
What if I put in all this time,

00:13:44.482 --> 00:13:45.942
and become an excellent employee,

00:13:45.942 --> 00:13:47.280
and I don't get promoted?

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:49.320
What if, I put in all this work,

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.350
to become an excellent
salesman, and I don't sell?

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.517
What if, what if, what if?

00:13:55.592 --> 00:13:57.752
And I tell ya, what if.

00:13:57.752 --> 00:13:59.682
What if, you don't do sh**?

00:13:59.682 --> 00:14:01.272
Where are you going to be?

00:14:01.272 --> 00:14:02.451
'Cause, it isn't going to be any better

00:14:02.451 --> 00:14:04.886
than where you are now.

00:14:04.886 --> 00:14:05.719
Alright?

00:14:06.886 --> 00:14:08.740
It's very easy for people,

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:11.959
who are in the beginning
levels of success,

00:14:11.959 --> 00:14:14.792
or the beginning levels
of their success journey,

00:14:14.792 --> 00:14:17.042
to tell themselves stories,

00:14:18.576 --> 00:14:21.946
that other people's circumstances
are better than theirs,

00:14:21.946 --> 00:14:25.885
that the other people have rich parents,

00:14:25.885 --> 00:14:29.115
they've got luck, they've
got better circumstances.

00:14:29.115 --> 00:14:31.426
They got less obstacles.

00:14:31.426 --> 00:14:34.264
And they say, and I understand, you know,

00:14:34.264 --> 00:14:37.065
that if you just do the
work, you'll get the result.

00:14:37.065 --> 00:14:38.897
But, what if?

00:14:38.897 --> 00:14:41.024
Okay, they want to believe
it, they want to succeed,

00:14:41.024 --> 00:14:42.476
but at the end of the day,

00:14:42.476 --> 00:14:44.316
they don't f****** do it,

00:14:44.316 --> 00:14:46.655
because they talk themselves out of it.

00:14:46.655 --> 00:14:47.488
Alright?

00:14:49.313 --> 00:14:51.282
This is easily the number one thing,

00:14:51.282 --> 00:14:52.802
that keeps people from succeeding.

00:14:52.802 --> 00:14:53.952
It's the number one thing,

00:14:53.952 --> 00:14:55.313
that keeps people where they are.

00:14:55.313 --> 00:14:58.143
It's the number one thing,
that keeps people broke.

00:14:58.143 --> 00:15:01.231
It's the number one thing, that
keeps people in a situation,

00:15:01.231 --> 00:15:02.981
of frustration, or...

00:15:05.013 --> 00:15:07.222
(clears throat) Basically, regret.

00:15:07.222 --> 00:15:10.162
And what ends up happening is,

00:15:10.162 --> 00:15:13.094
is that they end up
going through their life,

00:15:13.094 --> 00:15:18.043
accepting what they're dealt,
doing what they're told,

00:15:18.043 --> 00:15:20.414
and they end up at 50, 60 years old,

00:15:20.414 --> 00:15:22.884
wondering what the f*** happened.

00:15:22.884 --> 00:15:25.293
Well, I'm going to tell you what happened.

00:15:25.293 --> 00:15:26.741
You talked yourself out of going after

00:15:26.741 --> 00:15:28.492
what you were supposed to go after.

00:15:28.492 --> 00:15:30.512
You talked yourself out of your purpose.

00:15:30.512 --> 00:15:33.014
You talked yourself out of the idea,

00:15:33.014 --> 00:15:36.711
that success is cause and
effect, not magic luck,

00:15:36.711 --> 00:15:38.882
or magic fairy dust.

00:15:38.882 --> 00:15:41.373
That's what happened, okay?

00:15:41.373 --> 00:15:42.563
And that's the number one thing,

00:15:42.563 --> 00:15:44.252
that keeps people from succeeding.

00:15:44.252 --> 00:15:47.073
It's the what if story,
that they tell themselves,

00:15:47.073 --> 00:15:48.832
over, and over, and over again,

00:15:48.832 --> 00:15:52.423
as to why they can't move
forward, and other people can.

00:15:52.423 --> 00:15:55.171
Why, if they do the work, it
still isn't going to work out.

00:15:55.171 --> 00:15:56.773
Success is easy, guys!

00:15:56.773 --> 00:15:58.762
It's f****** easy!

00:15:58.762 --> 00:16:02.581
It's making a plan, and
executing the plan, every day.

00:16:02.581 --> 00:16:04.114
It's that easy.

00:16:04.114 --> 00:16:05.374
It's that easy.

00:16:05.374 --> 00:16:06.552
Okay, and people will always be like,

00:16:06.552 --> 00:16:08.024
Andy, it's not that easy!

00:16:08.024 --> 00:16:09.222
There's got to be luck to it!

00:16:09.222 --> 00:16:11.271
You know, f******, my friend,

00:16:11.271 --> 00:16:14.403
he created the super
snuggy snowball machine,

00:16:14.403 --> 00:16:16.952
and it made 100 million
dollars, in one day!

00:16:16.952 --> 00:16:20.472
Well, you ain't your f****** friend!

00:16:20.472 --> 00:16:21.944
You're a regular dude, just like me,

00:16:21.944 --> 00:16:23.468
and I'm tellin' you, and
you can choose to believe

00:16:23.468 --> 00:16:24.817
whatever the f*** you want to believe,

00:16:24.817 --> 00:16:26.768
but the reality is this.

00:16:26.768 --> 00:16:28.779
Make a plan, work the plan.

00:16:28.779 --> 00:16:30.608
Make a plan, work the plan.

00:16:30.608 --> 00:16:32.329
Make a plan, work the plan.

00:16:32.329 --> 00:16:35.028
And whenever the plan doesn't work,

00:16:35.028 --> 00:16:37.220
you change the f****** plan!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.140
That's called failure!

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.167
It's called learning a lesson!

00:16:39.167 --> 00:16:40.668
It's called adjusting!

00:16:40.668 --> 00:16:43.367
On the run, you are not
going to have a perfect plan,

00:16:43.367 --> 00:16:47.079
from start to finish, just
because you thought of an idea.

00:16:47.079 --> 00:16:49.009
That's reality, okay?

00:16:49.009 --> 00:16:51.697
So, when we talk about the what if story,

00:16:51.697 --> 00:16:52.617
you're telling yourself,

00:16:52.617 --> 00:16:56.784
the what if story, you're trying
to justify your fear with,

00:16:57.810 --> 00:16:59.749
it's bullsh**.

00:16:59.749 --> 00:17:01.609
It's bullsh**.

00:17:01.609 --> 00:17:04.259
If you do the work, and you
do it for a long enough time,

00:17:04.259 --> 00:17:06.988
and you have at least
average intelligence,

00:17:06.988 --> 00:17:09.150
you will be successful.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:09.983
Period.

00:17:11.167 --> 00:17:12.717
End of story.

00:17:12.717 --> 00:17:14.720
Now, you can accept
that, or you can go out,

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:16.990
and you can look for all
the little exceptions.

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:20.008
You can look for the, you
know, the glory stories,

00:17:20.008 --> 00:17:23.709
the guys who make millions
of dollars, in one year,

00:17:23.709 --> 00:17:25.479
which they don't.

00:17:25.479 --> 00:17:28.689
You know, it doesn't
happen to the average guy.

00:17:28.689 --> 00:17:30.556
You go out there, and say,
oh they got lucky, look.

00:17:30.556 --> 00:17:31.876
That's all luck, it's all luck.

00:17:31.876 --> 00:17:33.565
Or, you can accept the fact,

00:17:33.565 --> 00:17:36.466
that for people who
don't get lucky, like us,

00:17:36.466 --> 00:17:38.145
that there is a way to still do it,

00:17:38.145 --> 00:17:41.405
which is to f****** make a
plan, and execute the plan,

00:17:41.405 --> 00:17:44.284
and do that relentlessly, consistently,

00:17:44.284 --> 00:17:46.185
over the course of f****** ten years,

00:17:46.185 --> 00:17:48.475
and you'll be where you want to be.

00:17:48.475 --> 00:17:50.115
Alright, I'm not a f****** smart person,

00:17:50.115 --> 00:17:51.805
I'm not overly intelligent.

00:17:51.805 --> 00:17:54.164
I just make a list every
day, and execute on it!

00:17:54.164 --> 00:17:56.335
I don't worry about what if.

00:17:56.335 --> 00:17:58.254
I don't think about, what if I do this,

00:17:58.254 --> 00:17:59.766
and it doesn't work out the way I want?

00:17:59.766 --> 00:18:01.836
I know that it'll work out in some way,

00:18:01.836 --> 00:18:06.596
and because I'm smart enough
to adjust to plan, on the way,

00:18:06.596 --> 00:18:08.984
I know that it will at
least end up somewhere close

00:18:08.984 --> 00:18:10.651
to where I want to be.

00:18:12.529 --> 00:18:13.866
It's not that hard.

00:18:13.866 --> 00:18:15.085
Quit over-complicating it.

00:18:15.085 --> 00:18:15.985
There are no what ifs.

00:18:15.985 --> 00:18:18.246
If you do the f****** work,
the result will be there,

00:18:18.246 --> 00:18:19.245
period.

00:18:19.245 --> 00:18:21.282
- Well, the last, and
the most valuable lesson,

00:18:21.282 --> 00:18:23.224
as an entrepreneur, I learned,

00:18:23.224 --> 00:18:26.753
was about the value of execution.

00:18:26.753 --> 00:18:28.524
Way too many people.

00:18:28.524 --> 00:18:30.923
Way too many people, spend too much time,

00:18:30.923 --> 00:18:32.793
thinking about the vision.

00:18:32.793 --> 00:18:36.473
We are taught, that you have
to build a better mouse trap.

00:18:36.473 --> 00:18:38.801
Every venture capitalist will tell you,

00:18:38.801 --> 00:18:40.624
that to be a successful entrepreneur,

00:18:40.624 --> 00:18:42.792
you need a breakthrough innovation.

00:18:42.792 --> 00:18:45.848
Well, you have to assume, none of us,

00:18:45.848 --> 00:18:47.378
or at least most of us,

00:18:47.378 --> 00:18:49.827
are not the smartest people in the world.

00:18:49.827 --> 00:18:53.749
There are lots and lots of
great, great inventors out there.

00:18:53.749 --> 00:18:56.207
How are we going to be the person,

00:18:56.207 --> 00:18:58.819
who's going to always
build a better mouse trap?

00:18:58.819 --> 00:19:00.445
Well, to be successful,

00:19:00.445 --> 00:19:02.404
you don't have to build
a better mouse trap.

00:19:02.404 --> 00:19:05.666
You just have to build
a different mouse trap.

00:19:05.666 --> 00:19:08.664
And as long as you're executing well,

00:19:08.664 --> 00:19:11.694
the business, all of this,
comes down to block and tackle.

00:19:11.694 --> 00:19:13.575
It's not about the great vision,

00:19:13.575 --> 00:19:16.634
it's always about the great execution.

00:19:16.634 --> 00:19:18.274
And you can always succeed,

00:19:18.274 --> 00:19:21.174
by out-executing your competitors,

00:19:21.174 --> 00:19:24.465
not necessarily having the best
product in the marketplace.

00:19:24.465 --> 00:19:26.596
And I think that Microsoft
is a great example,

00:19:26.596 --> 00:19:29.304
where they took a same product,

00:19:29.304 --> 00:19:30.833
that other people may have had,

00:19:30.833 --> 00:19:32.964
but they executed substantially better,

00:19:32.964 --> 00:19:35.446
and today, the market leader, in industry.

00:19:35.446 --> 00:19:36.566
- Thank you guys so much for watching!

00:19:36.566 --> 00:19:37.576
I hope you enjoyed.

00:19:37.576 --> 00:19:40.084
I'd love to know, what did
you take from this video,

00:19:40.084 --> 00:19:42.856
that you are going to
immediately, now apply,

00:19:42.856 --> 00:19:44.824
to your life, or your business somehow.

00:19:44.824 --> 00:19:46.283
Please, leave it down,
in the comments below.

00:19:46.283 --> 00:19:47.624
I'm really curious to find out.

